{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"EPIC PLAN REVIEW #1 -> BLOCK (4 blocking, 10 advisory). Remediated:\n - B1/B2/B3 (E2,F1): three ACs were literally truncated mid-sentence ('...selected by', '...sanitizers,', '...written before any'). Rewrote all three as verifiable end-state criteria.\n - B4 (G6): plan's Step 2 said 'extract field maps, sanitizers' without acknowledging ADR 0035 SS(a) location-pinned files. VERIFIED the finding against the repo: adf.py / outbound_fields.py / comment_limits.py are loaded BY PATH and live (inbound_fields.py:36; outbound_fields.py:69 lazy_load('adapters/jira/adf.py'); tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_config.py:193; tests/integration/.../test_reconcile_roundtrip.py:72; tests/interfaces/store/test_commits_on_ticket.py:121; ~9 test files for comment_limits). Rewrote Step 2 to split movable vs pinned symbols and to share the pinned ones by DEPENDENCY INVERSION rather than relocation; added out-of-scope statement + an AC that no pinned module changes path and _loader.py is untouched.\n - Applied advisories: ADV5 (machine-checked import contract for the jira_family boundary), ADV6 (explicitly reject atlassian-python-api, per ADR 0004 survey), ADV7 (require https for DC base_url unless allow_insecure), ADV8 (least-privilege service-account PAT scope).\n - ADV10 judged already satisfied transitively (J5->J6->J7->J8 ordering).\nALSO fixed story J2 62d9 directly, which had a worse defect than the advisory flagged: its move set listed outbound_fields.py + comment_limits.py and claimed 'none of these modules is reached by lazy_load/spec_from_file_location' — FALSE per the greps above. Narrowed J2's move set to the three modules with ZERO by-path refs (jira_fields.py, identity.py, probe.py — verified), documented the pinned trio as dependency-inverted, and fixed ADV9's forward-referencing AC (the jira_datacenter grep check moves to J7).\nNOTE: value maps _LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA/_LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA live in movable jira_fields.py; the similarly-named _LOCAL_TO_JIRA_STATUS/_LOCAL_TO_JIRA_PRIORITY live in PINNED outbound_fields.py. Distinct symbols — do not conflate."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785288562593231001,"uuid":"99070cfc-3f36-40e8-acc8-5624805d4954"}